// @error Unterminated template literal
// @error-at 8
// An unterminated template reports AT ITS OPENING BACKTICK, not wherever the
// scan ran out. A `"` string ends at a raw newline, but a template does not —
// multiline is the point — so the scan runs to end of input and the position it
// stops at says nothing useful. The opening backtick is kept on a stack for
// exactly this, and popped when the template closes.
const s = `abc
print(s)
